  "question": {
    "text": "If $z_1$ and $z_2$ are two non-zero complex numbers such that $\\left|z_1+z_2\\right|=\\left|z_1\\right|+\\left|z_2\\right|$ then $\\arg z_1-\\arg z_2$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ZB5FS",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "BIzeM",
      "text": "\n$-\\pi$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "pRnU7",
      "text": "\n0\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "9otv6",
      "text": "\n$-\\frac{\\pi}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\left|z_1+z_2\\right|=\\left|z_1\\right|+\\left|z_2\\right| \\Rightarrow z_1$ and $z_2$ are collinear and are to the same side of origin; hence $\\arg z_1-\\arg z_2=0$.",
    "image": null
  },
